// A hiding commitment to a value under a blinding factor, the leaf a shielded note
// commits on chain. The value and its blinding are absorbed into the MiMC permutation,
// so the output reveals nothing about either yet binds them: no second (value, blinding)
// yields the same commitment without breaking the permutation. This is one of the two
// zKolang utilities the kernel exposes to NOX, a note a spender can later prove owning.
// Run: zkolang commitment.zkl
include "hash.zkl";

input value;
secret blinding;

output permute(value + blinding);
